1. Leave your known-payment filter separate

Your current Get_items filter is:

CCSubcategory ne 'Capital One Payment'

If this is still a known QuickBooks exclusion, you can leave it there.

But if accounting wants to also see those stripped rows in the negative-amount email, then you must remove it from Get_items and handle it later. Based on your correction, I would keep known-payment filtering separate from the negative amount reporting.

2. Add action: Filter_array_-_QBO_Upload_Rows

Add this after Apply_to_each.

Action type:

Data Operations → Filter array

Rename it to:

Filter_array_-_QBO_Upload_Rows

In From, use expression:

@body('Get_items')?['value']

Click Edit in advanced mode and use this expression:

@greaterOrEquals(
  add(
    if(empty(item()?['Debit']), 0, float(item()?['Debit'])),
    if(empty(item()?['Credit']), 0, float(item()?['Credit']))
  ),
  0
)
What this does

This keeps only rows where:

Debit + Credit >= 0

These rows will go into the QBO upload file.

3. Update existing action: Create_CSV_table

Open your existing Create_CSV_table.

Change From.

Current value:

@body('Get_items')?['value']

Replace it with:

@body('Filter_array_-_QBO_Upload_Rows')
4. Fix Line.Amount in existing Create_CSV_table

In Create_CSV_table, find the column:

Line.Amount

Current value:

@{item()?['Debit']}@{item()?['Credit']}

Replace it with this exact expression:

@{add(
  if(empty(item()?['Debit']), 0, float(item()?['Debit'])),
  if(empty(item()?['Credit']), 0, float(item()?['Credit']))
)}

This makes Line.Amount a real calculated value instead of concatenating Debit and Credit as text.

5. Add action: Filter_array_-_Negative_Line_Amount_Rows

Add another Filter array action after Apply_to_each.

Action type:

Data Operations → Filter array

Rename it to:

Filter_array_-_Negative_Line_Amount_Rows

In From, use:

@body('Get_items')?['value']

Click Edit in advanced mode and use this expression:

@less(
  add(
    if(empty(item()?['Debit']), 0, float(item()?['Debit'])),
    if(empty(item()?['Credit']), 0, float(item()?['Credit']))
  ),
  0
)
What this does

This captures rows where:

Debit + Credit < 0

These rows are stripped from the QBO upload but preserved for the accounting email.

6. Add action: Create_CSV_table_-_Negative_Line_Amount_Rows

Add this after:

Filter_array_-_Negative_Line_Amount_Rows

Action type:

Data Operations → Create CSV table

Rename it to:

Create_CSV_table_-_Negative_Line_Amount_Rows

Set From to:

@body('Filter_array_-_Negative_Line_Amount_Rows')

Set Columns to:

Custom

Add these columns:

Header	Value
SharePoint ID	@{item()?['ID']}
Transaction Date	@{item()?['Transaction_x0020_Date']}
Cardholder	@{item()?['Cardholder']?['DisplayName']}
Description	@{item()?['Description']}
Category	@{item()?['CCCategory']}
Subcategory	@{item()?['CCSubcategory']}
Debit	@{item()?['Debit']}
Credit	@{item()?['Credit']}
Calculated Line Amount	@{add(if(empty(item()?['Debit']), 0, float(item()?['Debit'])), if(empty(item()?['Credit']), 0, float(item()?['Credit'])))}
Client Name	@{item()?['Client_x0020_Name']}
Comments	@{item()?['Comments']}
7. Add action: Send_email_-_Negative_Line_Amount_Rows_to_Accounting

Add this after:

Create_CSV_table_-_Negative_Line_Amount_Rows

Action type:

Office 365 Outlook → Send an email (V2)

Rename it to:

Send_email_-_Negative_Line_Amount_Rows_to_Accounting

Use this recipient, unless accounting gives you a better distribution list:

dfriedrichs@mailctp.com

Subject:

Capital One QBO Upload - Negative Line Amounts Stripped Out - @{body('Convert_time_zone')}

Body:

<p>Hello,</p>

<p>The attached transactions were stripped out of the Capital One QBO upload because their calculated Line Amount was negative.</p>

<p><strong>Rule used:</strong> Debit + Credit &lt; 0</p>

<p>These transactions were not included in the QBO upload CSV file.</p>

<p>Please review the attached CSV for the stripped-out line transactions.</p>

<p>Thank you.</p>

Attachment Name:

Negative_Line_Amounts_Stripped_Out_@{body('Convert_time_zone')}.csv

Attachment Content:

@{base64(body('Create_CSV_table_-_Negative_Line_Amount_Rows'))}
8. Important: control the run order

Set these run orders:

Existing QBO upload path

Create_CSV_table should run after:

Filter_array_-_QBO_Upload_Rows

Not directly after Apply_to_each.

Negative email path

Create_CSV_table_-_Negative_Line_Amount_Rows should run after:

Filter_array_-_Negative_Line_Amount_Rows

Send_email_-_Negative_Line_Amount_Rows_to_Accounting should run after:

Create_CSV_table_-_Negative_Line_Amount_Rows
9. Optional but recommended: only send accounting email if negative rows exist

Wrap the negative email branch in a Condition.

Add a Condition after:

Filter_array_-_Negative_Line_Amount_Rows

Condition expression:

@greater(length(body('Filter_array_-_Negative_Line_Amount_Rows')), 0)

If Yes:

Create_CSV_table_-_Negative_Line_Amount_Rows
Send_email_-_Negative_Line_Amount_Rows_to_Accounting

If No:

Do nothing

This prevents accounting from receiving empty emails.

